B.agb=new A.en(["open","\ud83d\udcb0","Start low, but not too low","Stallholders always ask more than they expect to get. Open at about two-thirds of their price and come up a little each time. Far too low makes them cross.",'"Auntie, $12 can or not?"',"Close a deal well below the first price."])
B.ag7=new A.en(["compliment","\ud83d\ude0d","Say something nice","A kind word about their goods (or their stall) puts them in a better mood, and a happy stallholder comes down more. Try one sincere compliment first. Auntie Mei catches on quickly if you repeat yourself.",'"Wah, your mangoes look so sweet today!"',"Be nice before you talk price."])
B.ag5=new A.en(["regular","\ud83d\ude4b","Be a regular","Stallholders look after their regulars. Saying you come every week helps, and coming back often really does make them your friend (hearts \ud83d\udc9b).",'"I buy from you every week one!"',"Tell them you come here often."])
B.agg=new A.en(["competitor","\ud83d\udc40","Mention a cheaper stall","Saying the stall next door is cheaper can make them drop the price to keep you. Say it early, while their price is still high: near their lowest it only annoys them (stubborn ones sooner).",'"The one over there selling cheaper leh."',"Let them know there are other stalls."])
B.ag8=new A.en(["bulk","\ud83d\udecd\ufe0f","Buy two","Asking for a price for two gets a better price for each one. Good when you need more than one anyway. Not for one-of-a-kind things (antiques, pre-loved, legendary): there is only one!",'"If I take two, how much?"',"Ask about buying more than one."])
B.agl=new A.en(["budget","\ud83d\udc5b","Name your budget","Telling them how much you have makes them decide if they can meet you there. Use a believable number.",'"I only got $15 leh."',"Tell them how much you can spend."])
B.aga=new A.en(["plead","\ud83e\udd7a","Ask nicely for a discount",'Sometimes a polite "can cheaper?" is all it takes. Ask once or twice; beg too much and they get tired of it.','"Auntie, can give a bit of discount or not?"',"Just ask, politely."])
B.agd=new A.en(["final","\ud83e\uddf1","Know a last price","When they say it's their last price, offering lower again only uses up patience. Take it, or walk away.",'"OK lah, deal!"',"Haggle until they say it's their last price."])
B.agn=new A.en(["walk","\ud83d\udeb6","Walk away","Near their last price, after a friendly chat, walking away can get you called back with a better price. Rude or far apart, and they just let you go.",'"Never mind, I look around first."',"Get called back after walking away."])
B.agc=new A.en(["patience","\u2764\ufe0f","Watch their patience","Every move uses up a bit of patience (the hearts at the top). When it runs out, there's no sale. Don't drag it out with tiny steps.",'"OK OK, last one: $14?"',"Play a few haggles, or see what happens when patience runs out."])
B.agj=new A.en(["softspot","\ud83d\udca1","Find their soft spot","Every stallholder loves talking about something (Uncle Lim's fishing trips, Auntie Mei's grandson). Find it and they warm up a lot. Their profile has clues.",'"Uncle, you still go fishing on weekends?"',"Chat about what they love. Their profile has clues."])
B.ag4=new A.en(["tagteam","\ud83e\udd1c","Tag team","Haggling with a friend: one sweet-talks, the other makes the offer. The stallholder can't help being charmed.",'(Friend) "So nice your stall!"  (You) "$12 can?"',"Haggle together with a friend (\ud83d\udc65)."])
