B.a9Z=new A.ad(B.aaY,["You greet the customer and say the asking price.","The customer offered {offer}. You refuse it but come down to {ask}.","The customer offered {offer}. You won't go lower than {ask}. If they said that's all they have, say kindly you understand but still can't.","The customer offered only {offer}, which is far too low: it offends you. Show clearly that you're offended (not just 'not enough'), in character and without being nasty; your price stays {ask}.","The customer confirmed: sold at {deal}. Close the deal happily.","You agree to sell at {deal}, but the customer has NOT confirmed yet. Say yes happily, then END with a question asking them to confirm at {deal} (e.g. '..., deal or not?'). Don't say it's sold or wrap it yet.","The customer isn't ready to confirm yet. Tell them to take their time; the price is still {ask}.","The customer complimented you or your goods. You're pleased and say {ask}.","The customer keeps sweet-talking. You're tired of it and want them to buy.","The customer says another stall is cheaper. You grumble but lower to {ask}.","The customer says another stall is cheaper. You're annoyed and keep {ask}.","The customer will buy two. You give {ask} each.","The customer just repeated the same offer ({offer}). You hold at {ask}, a little impatient: tell them to come up a bit.","The customer wants to buy two, but you only have this one. Tell them so; the price for it is still {ask}.","The customer changed their mind: they want just one now, not two. That's fine, but the price for one is {ask}.","The customer says they're a regular. You warm up and say {ask}.","The customer is chatting. Chat back briefly; the price is still {ask}.","The customer asks for a cheaper price. You sigh and come down a little to {ask}.","The customer keeps asking for cheaper without naming a price. You hold at {ask} and tell them to name a price.","The customer was rude. You're offended.","The customer flirted or said something creepy. Laugh it off politely, firmly NOT flirting back, and steer back to the goods; the price is still {ask}.","The customer is firm at {offer} (their limit). That's below what you can do today. Kindly tell them your best price for them is {ask}. Don't call it your cost price or your real lowest.","The customer told you a sad story. Show real sympathy, in character; your price is now {ask}.","The customer keeps telling sad stories. Stay kind but firm; your price is still {ask}.","You're not sure what the customer means ({unclear}). Ask them, in character, to say clearly; your price is still {ask}.","The customer is walking away. Call them back, in character, with your final-final price {ask}: say clearly it's truly your last price.","The customer walked away. You let them go.","You've run out of patience and won't sell to this customer today.","You didn't understand what price the customer means. Ask them to say a number."],t.l)
B.aa1=new A.ad(B.de,["You just walked up to the stall. Make your first offer: {offer}.","The seller asked {ask}. That is too much for you, but you go up to {offer}. Say so.","The seller asked {ask}, which you find outrageous. React, without making a new offer.","The seller asked {ask} and you agree to pay {price}. Close the deal happily.","The seller accepted your offer of {price}. Thank them.","The seller was friendly to you. Respond warmly and repeat your offer of {offer}.","The seller keeps chatting instead of naming a price. You are getting impatient: your offer is still {offer}.","You give up and walk away without buying. Say goodbye in character."],t.l)
